 "literal": "Clasp the attachment of Him who is without attachment; that attachment clasp, for attachments to be let go.",
 "translation": "Clasp the attachment of Him who is free from all attachments; hold fast to that attachment so that you may let go of your own attachments.",
 "modern": "பற்றுகள் இல்லாதவனுடைய பற்றினைப் பற்றிக் கொள்ளுங்கள்; நம்முடைய பற்றுகளை விடுவதற்காக அந்தப் பற்றினைப் பற்றிக் கொள்ளுங்கள்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet explains the path to complete renunciation through a beautiful play on the word 'patru', which means both 'attachment' and 'to hold fast'. The mind cannot remain entirely empty; to rid oneself of worldly desires, one must anchor the mind onto something that is completely free of attachments. By holding onto this pure, desireless attachment, one's own worldly bonds naturally fall away. Thus, the higher attachment becomes the tool to dissolve all lower attachments.",
